      "problem": "Evaluate $5\\times \\left(3+2^2\\right).$",
      "worked_solution": "According to PEMDAS, we should first calculate the expression inside the **P**arentheses: $\\left(3+2^2\\right).$\n\nTo evaluate $\\left(3+2^2\\right),$ we should again apply PEMDAS. We start with the **E**xponents:\n\n$$\n3\\,+\\overbrace{2^2}^{\\large\\color{blue} 4} =3+ {\\color{blue} 4}\n$$\n\nThen, we perform the **A**ddition:\n\n$$\n3 + 4 =  {\\color{red} 7}\n$$\n\nSo we have:\n\n$$\n5\\times \\underbrace{\\left(3+2^2\\right)}_{\\large\\color{red} 7}  =5\\times {\\color{red} 7}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow that we have calculated the expression inside the **P**arentheses, we can finally move on to the **M**ultiplication:\n\n$$\n5 \\times 7 = 35\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n5\\times\\left(3+2^2\\right)=35.\n$$",
